    "fonts": "Consumer-bounded font glyph pointer arrays. EncodeSmallFontString supplies the 45 small glyphs; byte-oriented character indexing supplies the 256-entry lookup. Original regional literal pools establish bases; full pointed-to renderer sprite payloads match by glyph index.",
    "regional_fonts": "Five font glyph tables exist only in US/JP. Their consumers are absent or select EU replacements. Full renderer-consumed sprite payloads match per glyph in US/JP; explicit absent raw-target names prevent invented EU interpolation.",
    "native_catalog": "The existing glyph-pointer tables and their companion one-entry animation indexes are a coherent generated font resource catalog. Each original glyph table is immediately followed by its AnimHeader pointer; independently, the last glyph sprite payload ends exactly where that pointer-target AnimHeader begins, and its existing one-frame animation references glyph zero. This pattern holds for all seven US/JP font resources and both EU resources. The glyph tables are consumed only by msg.c font readers; the companion animation indexes have no active C reader and remain preserved as resource metadata. Moving the existing indexes from generic card lookup/localized catalogs into this font catalog restores one native initialized-data run of 5224 bytes in US/JP and1212 bytes in EU. Existing types, qualifiers, bounds, regional identities and initializer tokens remain unchanged. The adjacent nonfont resource starting at gUnk_09EEC5F0 remains in its existing provider; no larger source boundary is asserted. All existing object contracts and glyph/animation asset payloads are preserved."
